{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CefiUZc8CJey6t26tWJnN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The work item is complete and closed. Summary:\n\n**WI-579 — the verdict carrier, tree identity, and the `adjudication_review` dial** (branch `wi-579-the-verdict-carrier-and-the-ad`, spec moved to `docs/archive/work/complete/`, close commit `0c7cb4eb` carrying `WI: WI-579`).\n\n**What shipped**\n\n- **`kitlib/verdict.py`** (LLR-207, IF-175) — one home for the verdict record: the non-record tree identity (SHA-256 fold of `git ls-tree -r` with `docs/reviews/`, `docs/log.d/`, `docs/iteration/` dropped), the `Review-Verdict:` trailer grammar, and the round-file ↔ session-log join. Two readers stand on it, which was the point: `integrate._verdict_gate` and `agent_loop.review_owed_by_evidence` had two rules over two exclusion sets, and the gap between them drew two identical rounds on WI-547.\n- **The gate** computes over round files restricted to rounds a *logged reviewer session* produced (closing finding K), governed by tree identity at the **work tip** — the freshness comparison retires, the refresh peel is inherited. It re-homes `score_reviews.latest_phase_verdicts`, which had been written \"for the integrator gate\" and had no caller.\n- **`[attestation] adjudication_review`** through one reader shared by the round scheduler and the gate. An adjudication lane drafting ordinary successors now merges with **no verdict artifact anywhere** — the OI-76 stopper.\n- **`gen_verdict_rollup.py`** — the rollup reborn generated, `--check`-gated, wired into `[generated]`, the trunk step, `check.py`, and the hook floor. A lane never commits one.\n- Migration window with a stderr WARN, two `RESYNC_PACK.md` entries, two `enforcement-audit.md` rows.\n\n**Two things worth flagging to you**\n\n1. **The full suite ends 3336 passed / 24 skipped / 1 failed.** The failure is `test_derive_stage.py::test_this_repo_s_committed_stage_is_current` — `docs/stage` freshness, a trunk-owned generated artifact a work branch must not commit. I bisected rather than assumed: it passes at the integration base `0ecc62bb`, so my spine edits moved the fingerprint and the trunk regen clears it. But that test has **no lane stand-down** the way `check.py`'s `derived-stage` step does, so *every* spine-touching lane reds on it and a real staleness is indistinguishable from this. Recorded as an out-of-scope finding in the log fragment; one guard fixes it.\n2. **A defect the tests caught in my own code:** both new readers asked drafts for `safety_class`, but `intake.parse_dispositions` normalizes that cell into `kind` — `when-minting` would have silently behaved as `never`. Found only because the test asserts the *other* answer beside the merge-with-no-verdict case.\n\nSpine rows are all `Drafted`, no `Status` flipped, no `last_approved` written, no coordination truth touched. Ratchet bumps (`agent_common`, `agent_loop`, `integrate`, `check`, `bootstrap`, smoke membership) each carry their reason; `_verdict_gate`'s complexity bump was refused and the function decomposed instead."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":374,"cache_read_input_tokens":415239,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":374},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7656580b-8bca-4af8-bd6c-df62ced3e1c9","uuid":"6ae6ab82-f706-4c8d-ad93-26d40c871a1d","request_id":"req_011CefiUUp9dsj7HAyoSSWdD"}
